---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { business } from '../config/business';

const title = 'Privacy | Sunshine Climate Solutions';
const description =
  'How Sunshine Climate Solutions handles your information: the request form, Web3Forms, optional Google Analytics, cookieless analytics, and how to reach us.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>How Your Information Is Handled</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Short version: this website runs no advertising or remarketing, Google Analytics is optional and off until you allow it, a cookieless analytics service measures visits without identifying you, and the only personal information we collect is what you choose to send us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What the request form collects</h2>
        <p>
          The service request form sends the information you type into it: your name, phone
          number, ZIP code, the service you selected, your description of the problem, and — only
          if you provide them — your email address, preferred date and time window, and a company
          or project name.
        </p>
        <p>
          We ask for a ZIP code to help confirm service coverage before we talk. We don't collect
          your street address through the form.
        </p>

        <h2>Campaign attribution</h2>
        <p>
          If you arrive from one of our campaign links — for example a post, an email, or a
          printed QR code — the site remembers the campaign information from that link (the
          platform, the campaign name, the page you landed on, an external referring site if
          there was one, and when the visit happened) in your browser's local storage. If you
          later send a service request, that campaign information is included with the request
          so we can see how customers find us. It contains no personal details and no form
          contents, it is never sent to Google Analytics or Umami, and it travels only as part
          of the request you choose to submit. You can clear it at any time by clearing your
          browser's site data.
        </p>

        <h2>How form submissions are processed</h2>
        <p>
          Submissions are transmitted to <a href="https://web3forms.com" rel="noopener">Web3Forms</a>,
          a third-party form-processing service. Web3Forms forwards the submission as an email to
          our business inbox ({business.email}) so we can follow up with you. Processing happens on
          Web3Forms' servers; this website itself has no database and stores nothing.
        </p>
        <p>
          For details about Web3Forms' own handling of submission data, refer to their published
          privacy documentation. If you prefer not to send information through a third-party form
          processor, call or text {business.phone.display} instead — that works just as well.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This site uses two analytics services: an optional one that runs only with your
          permission, and a cookieless one that never identifies you.
        </p>
        <h3>Google Analytics (optional — not loaded until you allow it)</h3>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics 4, delivered through Google Tag Manager, to understand which
          pages are visited and how often visitors use the call, text and request actions. It is
          entirely optional and starts unloaded: the Google Tag Manager container itself is not
          requested from Google until you choose "Allow analytics", so no analytics request
          reaches Google before that choice. On your first visit a banner asks; you can change
          your mind at any time with the "Analytics preferences" link in the footer of every
          page. Choosing "Reject" — or withdrawing permission later — keeps or returns analytics
          to the denied state and stops further measurement. A confirmed service request is
          counted only when analytics has been allowed.
        </p>
        <p>
          When allowed, Google Analytics uses cookies (named <code>_ga</code> and similar) and
          receives limited technical data — the page viewed, your approximate location derived
          from your IP address, and your device and browser type — to produce reports for us.
          Our event tracking sends fixed event names and a service category only; your name,
          phone number, email, ZIP code and anything you type into the form are never sent to
          Google. Advertising and personalization features are always denied: this site runs no
          ads and no remarketing. For details, see Google's privacy policy at{' '}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
        </p>
        <h3>Umami (cookieless)</h3>
        <p>
          This site also uses Umami Cloud, a lightweight analytics service, to understand how the
          site is used: which pages are visited and how often visitors use the call, text and
          request actions. These are recorded as simple counts under fixed event names (for
          example, "call-click"). No form contents, phone numbers, names or other personal
          information are ever sent to Umami.
        </p>
        <p>
          Umami does not use cookies and does not track visitors across websites. Like any web
          service, it processes limited technical data (such as the IP address a request comes
          from) to produce aggregate statistics. For details, see Umami's published privacy
          documentation at <a href="https://umami.is" rel="noopener">umami.is</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Beyond analytics, this site loads no advertising scripts. Fonts are served from this
          website's own files, so there are no third-party font or embedded-content requests.
        </p>

        <h2>Communication you start</h2>
        <p>
          If you call, text, or email us, we use your contact details to respond to your inquiry
          and coordinate service. That's it. We don't add customers to marketing lists through this
          website, and the form has no marketing sign-up checkbox.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this page? Email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>
          or call <a href={business.phone.href}>{business.phone.display}</a> and ask for the owner.
        </p>
        <p><em>Last updated: October 2026.</em></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
